! DF on a refill address, the last of Reference Manual p.32's class 3:
! the refills the VFL-FORMAT operations issue through progressive
! indexing.  Its two companions cover the operations p.32 names
! outright (df_refill_alarm.strap: R, RCZ) and the index-arithmetic
! and count-branch refills (df_refill_index_alarm.strap: CBR, V+CR,
! V+ICR, V-ICR).
!
!
! SUPERSEDED 2026-09-24, AND THE CORRECTION MATTERS MORE THAN THE
! PROGRAM.  The "weaker standard" note above rests on the claim that no
! listing here tests DF.  THAT CLAIM IS FALSE.  jb_ax5b routine 1260
! TEST 8C -- PDF pp.76-83, octal 022546.00-022732.40, labels
! 160127-160146 -- is a dedicated test of the DF AND IF INDICATORS
! under four enable/mask conditions, verified first-hand at 400 dpi:
!
!   160127 LVI,$X1,160AD1  -TEST 8C CHECKS DF + IF UNDER 4 CONDS,
!                          -1. DISABL MASK 0 FETCH OK IND NO INT
!                          -2. DIAABL MASK 1 FETCH OK NO IND NO INT
!                          -3. ENABLE MASK 0 FETCH OK IND ON NO INT
!                          -4. ENABLE MASK 1 NO FETCH IND ON INTRPT
!
! Condition 4 is the MASK-DEPENDENT half these programs scope out.  So
! this file was written to a weaker standard than was available, in a
! document this project had already read, thirty pages before the
! routine whose misreading produced the claim.  The program is not
! thereby wrong -- but it is not the strongest evidence available, and
! TEST 8C is the acceptance test it should be checked against.  See
! docs/NEXT.md item 2.
! WEAKER STANDARD, hand-written from p.32, for the reason
! df_data_fetch_alarm.strap states at length.
!
! FIVE SITES, TWO SHAPES, ACROSS TWO FUNCTIONS.  p.21 gives progressive indexing its
! refill: with the secondary operation V+ICR the index counts down and
! is refilled when the count reaches zero.  In this model L, + and K
! resolve that through a SHARED trailing block -- their own read never
! collides with a refill read, since they write only the accumulator
! and the indicators -- while ST and M+ resolve it INLINE in their own
! arms, because their completion is a storage write that cannot share
! an execute() call with a new read request.  Both shapes are below.
!
! THE INDEX VALUE POINTS OUTSIDE THE AREA AND THE REFILL FIELD POINTS
! INSIDE, which is what makes each block name one address.  A
! progressive VFL operation monitors its operand address too -- that is
! p.32 class 1, already covered -- so a value inside the area would
! light DF whether the refill signalled or not.  And for ST and M+ the
! operand address is a STORE, so a value inside the area would raise DS
! and interrupt as well.
!
! THE COUNT-FIVE BLOCK IS THE GATE, same as its companions: a refill
! that does not happen reads nothing, and p.32 monitors addresses
! "actually used".  In the shared trailing block that gate matters
! twice over, because that block runs for EVERY progressive VFL
! operation whether it refills or not.
!
! MASK-ZERO ONLY, same scope and reason as the companions.
!
! Instructions: BD, BE, LVI, SV, LX, L(V+ICR), ST(V+ICR), M+(V+ICR),
! CT0110(V+ICR), CM1111(V+ICR), BB, BB1, BBZ, BZB, B, BEW -- all
! implemented.

        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, RFSRC
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := RFSRC
        LVI, $X13, ABOVE
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := ABOVE
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit := 0: signal INSIDE
        BBZ, 12.20, $+1.0            ! DF's mask bit := 0
        BE,  $+.32
!
! ---- 1. L, the shared trailing block, count 1 -> 0 ---------------
        LX,  $X7,  PK1               ! value -> DATAW (outside), count 1,
                                     !   refill -> RFSRC (inside)
        L(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X7), 0
        BZB, $DF,  $                 ! hang if the refill address missed DF
        BB,  $IF,  $                 ! hang if it lit bit 21 instead of 20
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
!
! ---- 2. the same, count 5: no refill, so nothing to monitor ------
        LX,  $X7,  PK5
        L(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X7), 0
        BB,  $DF,  $                 ! hang if a refill that never happened
                                     !   lit DF -- and this block also pins
                                     !   that the trailing block does not
                                     !   signal for a progressive operation
                                     !   with no refill at all
!
! ---- 3. ST, the inline shape ------------------------------------
        LX,  $X8,  PK1
        ST(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X8), 0
        BZB, $DF,  $                 ! hang if ST's inline refill missed DF
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        BB,  6.0,  $                 ! and the STORE itself must not have
                                     !   signalled: DATAW is outside
!
! ---- 4. M+, the same inline shape -------------------------------
        LX,  $X9,  PK1
        M+(V+ICR)(BU,64,8), 0($X9), 0
        BZB, $DF,  $                 ! hang if M+'s inline refill missed DF
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        BB,  6.0,  $
!
! ---- 5. CT, the CONNECTIVE form of the shared trailing block -----
!   connectiveOp carries its own copy of that block, so vflIntOp's
!   count-five check above says nothing about this one.
        LX,  $X10, PK1
        CT0110(V+ICR)(BU,64), 0($X10), 0
        BZB, $DF,  $                 ! hang if CT's refill missed DF
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
!
! ---- 6. and that block's own count gate -------------------------
        LX,  $X10, PK5
        CT0110(V+ICR)(BU,64), 0($X10), 0
        BB,  $DF,  $
!
! ---- 7. CM, the connective inline shape -------------------------
!   CM writes its field back, so p.32 puts THAT address on the DS
!   side; only the refill address below can raise DF.
        LX,  $X11, PK1
        CM1111(V+ICR)(BU,64), 0($X11), 0
        BZB, $DF,  $                 ! hang if CM's inline refill missed DF
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        BB,  6.0,  $                 ! and CM's own write must not signal
        B,   PASS
PASS    BEW, $
!
! ---- constants, all OUTSIDE the monitored area -------------------
        SLC, (8)4200.0
PK1     XW, DATAW, 1, RFSRC          ! count 1: the refill fires
PK5     XW, DATAW, 5, RFSRC          ! count 5: it must not
DATAW   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525252525240
!
! ---- the monitored area ------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)4300.0
RFSRC   XW, (8)123456.76, (8)543210, (8)123456   ! == the lower boundary
ABOVE   DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! == the upper boundary, first word out
!
! ---- the interruption table --------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)4500.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, (8)4523.0
DSRTN   BB1, 6.0, $+1.0              ! entry 19 = DS
        END, START
